        [
          "✅ 1. Core Concept"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80ac-bacb-dcec4380589f",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What is it?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80bd-ad5f-ee2d92ecf7af",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "REST API validation ensures that the data a client (like a frontend app or another system) sends to your Spring Boot backend is valid and safe "
        ],
        [
          "before",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " your logic processes it. JSR-380 (Java Specification Request) is a standard for Java Bean Validation — think of it as adding rules directly on your class fields (like saying a field "
        ],
        [
          "must not be null",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ")."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80d7-a1f3-eb06809c70f9",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Why does it exist?",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8006-aec5-fe646a41dfb5",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "To "
        ],
        [
          "prevent bad data",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " (like empty names, null emails, or too-short passwords) from causing errors or saving incorrect info into your database. It improves "
        ],
        [
          "security, reliability, and user feedback",
          [
            [
              "b"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
