    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-80a2-971d-f11e57b8d8f9",
      "type": "quote",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Q: How does Spring Boot validate REST API input?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20924eb1-ed54-8059-a9c9-c57cf89b5a94",
      "type": "text",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot uses JSR-380 Bean Validation, which allows you to annotate fields in a DTO class with constraints like "
        ],
        [
          "@NotNull",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", "
        ],
        [
          "@Size",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", or "
        ],
        [
          "@Email",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ". When a REST controller method uses "
        ],
        [
          "@Valid",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          ", Spring checks the incoming data against these rules before running the method. If validation fails, it returns a "
        ],
        [
          "400 Bad Request",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " with the error. You can customize validation messages and handle errors globally for consistency."
        ]
